      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# dsh-plugin-grok2api-media-tool bundle patch layer.\n#\n# This file is what makes the plugin mount at all: `dsh plugin add` reads the\n# package's `dsh.bundle.patch` pointer to decide the package joins\n# `dsh.profile.bundles`, and the profile loader then applies the row below to\n# create the loader entry. Removing it turns the package into an inert library.\n#\n# The layer is applied after every bundle listed before it in\n# dsh.profile.bundles and before the profile's own cordis.patch.yml.\n#\n# No `config` is set here on purpose: every field already has a schema default\n# (baseUrl http://127.0.0.1:8000, apiFlavor chenyme, …), and this file lives\n# INSIDE the installed package — an edit here is overwritten by the next\n# `dsh plugin update`. Configure the plugin in one of these instead:\n#\n#   * in chat: \"把 grok2api 地址配成 …，密钥 …\" (the configure_grok2api tool),\n#   * $DSH_HOME/settings.yaml, `grok2api-media-tool:` section (hot-reloaded, no restart),\n#   * the profile's own cordis.patch.yml, by targeting `id: grok2api-media-tool` — note a\n#     patch REPLACES the row's whole config rather than merging into it.\n- insert:\n    - id: grok2api-media-tool\n      name: 'dsh-plugin-grok2api-media-tool'\n"
    }
